      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-110388",
      ":question/problem": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two independent continuous random variables whose marginal density functions are as follows:\n\n$f_{X}(x) = {4x^{3},\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le x \\le 1, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwisef_{Y}(y) = {\\frac{2}{3}y,\\begin{vmatrix}1 \\le y \\le 2, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$\n\nFind the joint probability density function $f(x, y)$."
